# The frontend reads three settings. Next loads them from .env.local (or the
# process environment); start.ps1 sets both itself.

# Where server-rendered pages reach the read API. The browser always uses the
# relative /vndbserve; this is the server's way to the same edge. A deployment
# points it at its own edge; start.ps1 points it at the edge it starts,
# unless the environment already names one.
NEOVNDB_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:17030/vndbserve

# 1 draws the site without requesting a single cover or screenshot (the boxes
# keep their size). Read at build time; start.ps1 -NoImages sets it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_NO_IMAGES=

# The dev server serves its scripts only to the hosts it knows: localhost and
# this machine's own addresses, so a phone on the same network can open
# http://<this machine's LAN address>:17030. A name the site is reached by
# besides those (a hostname, a tunnel) goes here, comma-separated. Without it
# such a visitor sees the text but no images, and cannot sign in.
NEOVNDB_DEV_ORIGINS=
